@page "/documentation"

<PageTitle>Documentation</PageTitle>

<section class="page-header">
    <p class="dashboard-label">User Guide</p>
    <h1>Application Documentation</h1>
    <p>
        This page explains how to use the Fitness Nutrition Tracker application and provides
        a clear demo flow for the final project presentation.
    </p>
</section>

<section class="feature-grid">
    <div class="feature-card">
        <div class="feature-icon">🏠</div>
        <h3>Dashboard</h3>
        <p>
            The dashboard is the main entry point of the application. It connects users to nutrition,
            workouts, profile, goals, progress, and documentation.
        </p>
    </div>

    <div class="feature-card">
        <div class="feature-icon">🥗</div>
        <h3>Nutrition Diary</h3>
        <p>
            The nutrition section helps users register food, review nutrition data, and connect meal records
            with daily nutrition tracking.
        </p>
    </div>

    <div class="feature-card">
        <div class="feature-icon">🏋️</div>
        <h3>Workout Tracking</h3>
        <p>
            Users can add, edit, review, and delete workout records including exercise type,
            duration, date, and notes.
        </p>
    </div>

    <div class="feature-card">
        <div class="feature-icon">👤</div>
        <h3>User Profile</h3>
        <p>
            Users can save personal information such as name, starting weight, height, and age.
            This prepares the app for personalized health tracking.
        </p>
    </div>

    <div class="feature-card">
        <div class="feature-icon">🎯</div>
        <h3>Goals</h3>
        <p>
            The goals page organizes fitness and nutrition planning, including weight goals,
            nutrition goals, workout goals, and weekly review.
        </p>
    </div>

    <div class="feature-card">
        <div class="feature-icon">📈</div>
        <h3>Progress</h3>
        <p>
            The progress page provides a summary area for reviewing meals, workouts,
            completed goals, and future progress metrics.
        </p>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="feature-card">
    <h3>Final Demo Flow</h3>
    <p>
        Use the following order for the final presentation video:
    </p>

    <ol class="demo-list">
        <li>Open the Dashboard and explain the purpose of the application.</li>
        <li>Go to the Profile page and save basic user information.</li>
        <li>Go to Workouts and add a workout record.</li>
        <li>Show how the workout can be edited or deleted.</li>
        <li>Open the Nutrition Diary or Food Register section and explain the nutrition feature.</li>
        <li>Open Goals and explain how users can plan fitness and nutrition targets.</li>
        <li>Open Progress and explain how the app can summarize user activity.</li>
        <li>Finish with Documentation to show that the app includes a user guide.</li>
    </ol>
</section>

<section class="feature-card">
    <h3>Known Limitations and Future Improvements</h3>
    <ul class="clean-list">
        <li>Connect Progress page to real meal, workout, and goal data.</li>
        <li>Add persistent storage for workouts and profile data if needed.</li>
        <li>Add authentication for individual users.</li>
        <li>Improve charts and weekly progress history.</li>
        <li>Expand nutrition reports and daily summaries.</li>
    </ul>
</section>